{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/justify"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"justify","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"justify"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV7justifyAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgvp","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"justify","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"justify"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The justify attribute is used to indicate left, center, or right justification. The default value varies for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different elements. For elements where the justify attribute is present but the halign attribute is not, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"justify attribute indicates horizontal alignment as well as justification."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/justify"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displayed in the music notation.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLMetronome","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/justify":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The justify attribute is used to indicate left, center, or right justification. The default value varies for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different elements. For elements where the justify attribute is present but the halign attribute is not, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"justify attribute indicates horizontal alignment as well as justification."}],"title":"justify","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"justify"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/justify","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/justify"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLeftCenterRight":{"title":"MXLLeftCenterRight","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlleftcenterright","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","abstract":[{"text":"The left-center-right type is used to define horizontal alignment and text justification.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}